 # Changelog
 
+## 0.1.3 (unreleased)
+
+Additive. Code-only: nothing in this section was compiled or run when written.
+
+- `capture` module (#413): `WDA_NONE`, `WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE`, `NS_WINDOW_SHARING_NONE`, `NS_WINDOW_SHARING_READ_ONLY`, `windows_affinity` and `macos_sharing_type` map "exclude from capture" to the OS values. Pure and tested on every OS.
+- `windows::exclude_from_capture(hwnd, exclude)` (#413): `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` with `WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE`. The non-Windows stub returns `false`. The macOS `NSWindow.sharingType` call itself is not in Rust: it needs an Objective-C binding this crate does not depend on; the Swift overlay sets it using `capture::macos_sharing_type`.
+- `windows::covering_window(hwnd, own_pids)` (#525): the Windows z-order walk behind `covering_window`. It reads up to `MAX_COVERING_WALK` windows above, with class name, visibility, owning pid, `DWMWA_CLOAKED` and bounds. The non-Windows stub returns `None`. Enables the `Win32_Graphics_Dwm` windows-sys feature.
